          "text": "# Lakehouse Guardian A local Spark/Iceberg data-quality workflow with dbt checks, LangGraph approval gates, and measured fault-injection evaluations on UCI Bike Sharing data. [![Verification](https://github.com/Sunnyvulli/lakehouse-guardian/actions/workflows/verify.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/Sunnyvulli/lakehouse-guardian/actions/workflows/verify.yml) **Inspect in 60 seconds:** [recorded run](results/demo.json) \u00b7 [fault evaluation](results/evaluation.json) \u00b7 [failure analysis](docs/failure-analysis.md) \u00b7 [decisions](docs/decisions.md). This is a local reference system; AWS resources have not been applied. ## Quick start Python 3.12, Java 17, and GNU Make on Linux are the tested prerequisites. The first installation downloads Spark and scientific packages; no five-minute clean-OS promise is made. ```sh python3 -m venv .venv . .venv/bin/activate pip install -r requirements.txt make run ``` `make run` explicitly approves publication of the bundled, attributed local fixture. It executes an actual LangGraph interrupt/resume, Spark transformation, five dbt checks, and an Iceberg commit. It does not approve any cloud change. Run `python -m guardian.demo` without the approval flag to inspect the interrupted proposal with no publication. `make test eval` runs the behavioral tests"
